   {
    "title": "QuickTasks",
    "description": "Demo checklist app built on a custom-made MVC framework inspired by Rails, hosted on AWS EC2. \n\n• Light-weight ORM supports several ActiveRecord query and CRUD methods.\n• Backend features sessions, cached assets, view templates, & strong params.\n• Bcrypt-based authentication secures user credentials via salted password hash.\n\nGitHub: https://github.com/fndelacruz/quicktasks\n\nTechnologies used: Ruby, JavaScript, CSS, SQLite3, AWS",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "May 2016 - Present"
   },
   {
    "title": "SnackOverflow",
    "description": "Culinary Q&A inspired by StackOverflow, hosted on Heroku.\n\n• True SPA design using AJAX calls to a RESTful JSON API facilitates seamless authentication from any site component.\n• Model relationships and custom SQL methods eliminate N+1 queries and minimize unnecessary calls to the databases.\n• Site content procedurally generated using Markov Chain models trained on data fetched via StackExchange API and raw HTML scraping.\n\nTechnologies used: Ruby on Rails, ReactJS, PostgreSQL, jQuery, CSS, StackExchange API\n\nGithub: https://github.com/fndelacruz/snackoverflow/",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Apr 2016 - Present"
   }
